Bugfix: Return 400 instead of 500 when user-provided storage credentials are rejected

The files_external endpoint that saves a user's own credentials for an admin-defined
mount (PUT /apps/files_external/userglobalstorages/{id}) only handled "storage not
found". When the authentication mechanism rejected the submitted values (for example
an empty username or password, raised as InvalidArgumentException) or was left without
usable data (InsufficientDataForMeaningfulAnswerException), the request ended in a
500 server error without a message, so the Files credentials dialog and the personal
storage settings could not show the user what was wrong. Both cases now return
HTTP 400 with the reason.

